(MedEd-HalluScore v0.1) Tj
/F2 18 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 691 Tm
(A Practical Framework for Evaluating Hallucination and Educational) Tj
/F2 18 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 672 Tm
(Safety Risks in LLM-Generated Clinical Cases) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 625 Tm
(Author: Douglas Henrique Duarte) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 597 Tm
(Version: 0.1.0) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 569 Tm
(Date: 2026-05-09) Tj
/F2 18 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 541 Tm
(Abstract) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 494 Tm
(Large language models are increasingly capable of generating clinical cases for medical) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 480 Tm
(education. However, generated cases may contain factual errors, internal contradictions,) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 466 Tm
(missing safety-critical information, and misleading clinical reasoning. MedEd-HalluScore is) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 452 Tm
(a practical evaluation framework for scoring hallucination and educational safety risks in) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 438 Tm
(LLM-generated clinical cases. The framework uses six dimensions, each scored from 0 to 3,) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 424 Tm
(producing a total risk score from 0 to 18. This initial white paper describes the framework) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 410 Tm
(rationale, scoring method, intended use, limitations, and an initial validation plan.) Tj
/F2 18 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 382 Tm
(1. Background) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 335 Tm
(Clinical cases are central to medical education. They help learners practice diagnostic) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 321 Tm
(reasoning, identify relevant data, compare differential diagnoses, and connect clinical) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 307 Tm
(findings with management decisions. LLMs can accelerate case generation, but speed alone) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 293 Tm
(does not guarantee educational safety.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 265 Tm
(An AI-generated case may look fluent while containing incorrect facts, incoherent findings,) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 251 Tm
(omitted red flags, or unsafe teaching points. These failures are especially important in) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 237 Tm
(medical education because learners may not yet have enough expertise to recognize them.) Tj
/F2 18 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 209 Tm
(2. Objective) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 162 Tm
(MedEd-HalluScore aims to provide a structured, reproducible method for evaluating whether an) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 148 Tm
(LLM-generated clinical case is suitable for educational review and use.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 120 Tm
(The framework evaluates educational content. It is not designed for direct clinical care,) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 106 Tm
(diagnosis, treatment, triage, or patient-specific decision-making.) Tj
/F2 18 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 78 Tm
(3. Framework Design) Tj
ET
endstream
