(The framework includes six dimensions:) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 682 Tm
(1. Medical factuality) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 668 Tm
(2. Internal clinical consistency) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 654 Tm
(3. Critical information omissions) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 640 Tm
(4. Clinical reasoning risk) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 626 Tm
(5. Educational safety) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 612 Tm
(6. Transparency and verifiability) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 584 Tm
(Each dimension receives a score from 0 to 3:) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 556 Tm
(- 0: no apparent risk) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 542 Tm
(- 1: minor risk) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 528 Tm
(- 2: moderate risk) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 514 Tm
(- 3: severe risk) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 486 Tm
(The total score is the sum of all six dimensions.) Tj
/F2 18 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 458 Tm
(4. Risk Classification) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 411 Tm
(Total Score | Risk Level | Recommended Action) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 383 Tm
(0-3 | Low Risk | Use after routine human review and minor edits.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 369 Tm
(4-8 | Moderate Risk | Use only after careful correction and qualified review.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 355 Tm
(9-13 | High Risk | Do not use without substantial revision and re-review.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 341 Tm
(14-18 | Critical Risk | Reject or fully rewrite before educational use.) Tj
/F2 18 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 313 Tm
(5. Example Application) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 266 Tm
(A chest pain case that describes crushing substernal pain radiating to the left arm but) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 252 Tm
(omits vital signs, ECG, and troponin, then recommends discharge with antibiotics, would) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 238 Tm
(likely score high or critical risk. The issue is not only factual error, but also the) Tj
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 224 Tm
(possibility of teaching an unsafe reasoning pattern.) Tj
